title: ch2_resale_jacket
---
A real 1990s varsity jacket lands on your counter. You paid fifteen dollars for it at an estate sale. #line:ch2_resale_jacket_01
Online, the same jacket goes for anywhere between forty and a hundred and twenty. #line:ch2_resale_jacket_02
-> Check what actually sold, then price it. #line:ch2_resale_jacket_03
    <<choose "research">>
    Sold listings say eighty. It goes in four days at eighty. #line:ch2_resale_jacket_04
-> Tag it at forty and move it fast. #line:ch2_resale_jacket_05
    <<choose "quick">>
    Gone in an hour. The buyer relists it the same night for a hundred. #line:ch2_resale_jacket_06
===

title: ch2_resale_fake
---
A guy offers you ten designer bags for two hundred dollars. The stitching is a little too perfect. #line:ch2_resale_fake_01
Sell them as real and you could clear two thousand. #line:ch2_resale_fake_02
-> Refuse. Your shop sells real things. #line:ch2_resale_fake_03
    <<choose "refuse">>
    He shrugs and tries the next store. Word gets around that you don't play. #line:ch2_resale_fake_04
-> Buy them and say nothing. #line:ch2_resale_fake_05
    <<choose "buy">>
    The money is fast. A review calling your store a scam is faster. #line:ch2_resale_fake_06
===

title: ch2_resale_fakes_review
---
A customer posts a video taking the bag apart at the seams. Two hundred thousand views by lunch. #line:ch2_resale_fakes_review_01
-> Refund everyone and apologize publicly. #line:ch2_resale_fakes_review_02
    <<choose "refund">>
    It hurts. But the comments slowly change from scam to at least they owned it. #line:ch2_resale_fakes_review_03
-> Delete the comments and wait. #line:ch2_resale_fakes_review_04
    <<choose "deny">>
    The internet keeps screenshots. Foot traffic drops for weeks. #line:ch2_resale_fakes_review_05
===

title: ch2_resale_drop
---
You have a rack of rare sneakers. Jay says a Friday night drop on social media could pack the store. #line:ch2_resale_drop_01
-> Do the drop with Jay filming. #line:ch2_resale_drop_02
    <<choose "drop">>
    Jay: Told you. Line around the block. You owe me a slice. #line:ch2_resale_drop_03
-> List them online one by one. #line:ch2_resale_drop_04
    <<choose "list">>
    Steady sales, no crowd, no buzz. #line:ch2_resale_drop_05
===

title: ch2_resale_consign
---
A collector wants you to sell her closet on consignment. She keeps sixty percent, you keep forty. #line:ch2_resale_consign_01
No money up front, but the racks will be full of her clothes for months. #line:ch2_resale_consign_02
-> Take the consignment deal. #line:ch2_resale_consign_03
    <<choose "accept">>
    Her friends start dropping by. Some of them have closets too. #line:ch2_resale_consign_04
-> Offer to buy the best pieces outright. #line:ch2_resale_consign_05
    <<choose "buy">>
    You pay more today and keep every dollar of the markup. #line:ch2_resale_consign_06
===

title: ch2_resale_shoplifter
---
A teenager slips a beanie into his hoodie. You see it on the mirror. He sees you seeing it. #line:ch2_resale_shoplifter_01
-> Talk to him quietly. #line:ch2_resale_shoplifter_02
    <<choose "talk">>
    He puts it back. A week later he brings his older sister to shop. #line:ch2_resale_shoplifter_03
-> Call the police. #line:ch2_resale_shoplifter_04
    <<choose "police">>
    You lose the afternoon to a report about a twelve-dollar beanie. #line:ch2_resale_shoplifter_05
===
